From: RockBase SDK <dev@rockbase.local>
Subject: [PATCH] rtw88: usb: fix NULL chandef.chan deref panic on RX before start

RTL8821CU USB firmware starts delivering RX frames as soon as the bulk
IN URB is submitted during probe, before mac80211 calls hw_config to
assign hw->conf.chandef.chan. rtw_rx_fill_rx_status() then dereferences
a NULL chan and panics the kernel.

Drop RX frames while the device is not yet running (RTW_FLAG_RUNNING),
and guard the chan dereference in rtw_rx_fill_rx_status() as a second
line of defense covering all HCI paths.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rx.c
@@ -156,6 +156,8 @@
 	u8 path;
 
 	memset(rx_status, 0, sizeof(*rx_status));
+	if (!hw->conf.chandef.chan)
+		return;
 	rx_status->freq = hw->conf.chandef.chan->center_freq;
 	rx_status->band = hw->conf.chandef.chan->band;
 	if (rtw_fw_feature_check(&rtwdev->fw, FW_FEATURE_SCAN_OFFLOAD) &&
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
@@ -552,6 +552,11 @@
 		if (!skb)
 			break;
 
+		if (!test_bit(RTW_FLAG_RUNNING, rtwdev->flags)) {
+			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		rx_desc = skb->data;
 		chip->ops->query_rx_desc(rtwdev, rx_desc, &pkt_stat,
 					 &rx_status);
